From f6eed75a3176a86ec8a5b2883c718ff551263435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:10:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] CameraSource: fix CreateFromCamera surface parameter
 type

The camera HALv1 restoration reintroduced CreateFromCamera's
out-of-line definition using the pre-Flags.h sp<IGraphicBufferProducer>
type, but the header now declares it as sp<SurfaceType>, which resolves
to sp<Surface> when WB_LIBCAMERASERVICE_WITH_DEPENDENCIES is set. This
mismatch broke both the declaration/definition match and the
constructor call passing the producer where a Surface* was expected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I2d4cb46d5c6db0d76d096f987ebc16db50ed851f
---
 media/libstagefright/CameraSource.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/media/libstagefright/CameraSource.cpp b/media/libstagefright/CameraSource.cpp
index 56c3f9af1a..baac4a38d9 100644
--- a/media/libstagefright/CameraSource.cpp
+++ b/media/libstagefright/CameraSource.cpp
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ CameraSource *CameraSource::CreateFromCamera(
     pid_t clientPid,
     Size videoSize,
     int32_t frameRate,
-    const sp<IGraphicBufferProducer>& surface,
+    const sp<SurfaceType>& surface,
     bool storeMetaDataInVideoBuffers) {
 
     CameraSource *source = new CameraSource(camera, proxy, cameraId,
